    "gold_solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Modified_Facility_Location\")\n    m.setParam('TimeLimit', 300)\n\n    nf = 4\n    nc = 9\n    facility_coords = [(70, 88), (87, 85), (82, 53), (1, 31)]\n    customer_coords = [(95, 75), (30, 94), (30, 53), (19, 35), (1, 1), (53, 52), (34, 11), (37, 46), (2, 52)]\n    capacities = [158.0, 91.0, 103.0, 149.0]\n    demands = [23.0, 23.0, 32.0, 14.0, 47.0, 50.0, 20.0, 39.0, 12.0]\n    fixed_costs = [311.0, 421.0, 145.0, 309.0]\n    rate = 0.5\n\n    # Compute distances\n    dist = {}\n    for i in range(nf):\n        for j in range(nc):\n            dx = facility_coords[i][0] - customer_coords[j][0]\n            dy = facility_coords[i][1] - customer_coords[j][1]\n            dist[(i,j)] = math.sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy)\n\n    # Variables\n    open_f = {i: m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f'Open_F{i}') for i in range(nf)}\n    ship = {(i,j): m.addVar(lb=0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f'Ship_F{i}_C{j}')\n            for i in range(nf) for j in range(nc)}\n\n    # Objective\n    obj = quicksum(fixed_costs[i]*open_f[i] for i in range(nf))\n    obj += quicksum(dist[(i,j)]*rate*ship[(i,j)] for i in range(nf) for j in range(nc))\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # Demand satisfaction\n    for j in range(nc):\n        m.addConstr(quicksum(ship[(i,j)] for i in range(nf)) >= demands[j])\n\n    # Capacity linking\n    for i in range(nf):\n        m.addConstr(quicksum(ship[(i,j)] for j in range(nc)) <= capacities[i]*open_f[i])\n\n    # Policy: min throughput 19 per open facility\n    for i in range(nf):\n        m.addConstr(quicksum(ship[(i,j)] for j in range(nc)) >= 19.0*open_f[i])\n\n    # Policy: F3 requires F0\n    m.addConstr(open_f[3] <= open_f[0])\n\n    # Policy: at most 2 facilities open\n    m.addConstr(quicksum(open_f[i] for i in range(nf)) <= 2)\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "To: Operations Leadership Team\nFrom: Supply Chain Consulting\nSubject: Distribution Network Site Selection and Fulfillment Plan\n\nOverview\nWe are preparing a decision on which candidate distribution centers to activate and how to route product to customers so that all demand is fulfilled at the lowest total delivered cost. The decision balances two primary cost elements: the fixed expense of opening facilities and the variable cost of transportation driven by distance and volume. The analysis uses the facility and customer locations provided, each facility\u2019s available capacity, each customer\u2019s volume requirements, and a uniform per\u2011unit, per\u2011kilometer transport rate.\n\nBusiness Requirements\n- Service coverage: Every customer\u2019s demand must be fully satisfied.\n- Facility activation: Shipments may only depart from facilities that are opened, and opening any facility incurs its associated fixed cost.\n- Capacity discipline: Outbound shipments assigned to any facility must not exceed that facility\u2019s available capacity.\n- Transportation economics: Shipping costs scale with the distance traveled and the quantity shipped, using a consistent per\u2011unit, per\u2011kilometer rate.\n\nCompany Policies (mandatory)\n- Throughput threshold for activation: Any facility that is opened must handle at least 19 units of total outbound shipments across its assigned customers to justify operating overhead.\n- Dependency between specific sites: The location labeled F3 depends operationally on the regional hub labeled F0. If F3 is activated, F0 must also be activated.\n- Oversight limit on network size: To stay within management bandwidth, the company will operate no more than 2 distribution centers at any given time.\n\nDecision Goal\nSelect the set of distribution centers to activate (subject to the oversight limit and the F3\u2013F0 dependency), and assign customer volumes to the opened sites so that:\n- All customer demand is met without breaching any facility\u2019s capacity,\n- Every opened facility handles at least the minimum throughput noted above,\n- Total cost\u2014comprising facility opening costs and transportation costs based on distance and volume\u2014is minimized.\n\nApproach and Deliverables\n- We will evaluate feasible facility combinations that observe the two\u2011site operating limit and the F3\u2013F0 linkage, then allocate shipments from the opened facilities to customers in a way that fully meets demand and respects capacity and minimum\u2011throughput policies.\n- The recommended plan will specify which facilities to open, the customer coverage and shipment volumes from each opened site, and the resulting total cost broken down into fixed and transportation components.\n- We will also highlight the trade\u2011offs that drive the recommendation\u2014for example, when a higher\u2011fixed\u2011cost site could still be preferred due to lower aggregate transport costs\u2014and explain any cases where the minimum\u2011throughput requirement influences site selection.\n\nAnnex: Data Inputs\n- Candidate facility coordinates: Facility Coordinates:\n  - F0: (70, 88)\n  - F1: (87, 85)\n  - F2: (82, 53)\n  - F3: (1, 31)\n- Customer coordinates: Customer Coordinates:\n  - C0: (95, 75)\n  - C1: (30, 94)\n  - C2: (30, 53)\n  - C3: (19, 35)\n  - C4: (1, 1)\n  - C5: (53, 52)\n  - C6: (34, 11)\n  - C7: (37, 46)\n  - C8: (2, 52)\n- Facility capacities (units): [158.0, 91.0, 103.0, 149.0]\n- Customer demands (units): [23.0, 23.0, 32.0, 14.0, 47.0, 50.0, 20.0, 39.0, 12.0]\n- Facility opening fixed costs: [311.0, 421.0, 145.0, 309.0]\n- Transport rate (per kilometer per unit): 0.5",
    "LLM_description_template": "To: Operations Leadership Team\nFrom: Supply Chain Consulting\nSubject: Distribution Network Site Selection and Fulfillment Plan\n\nOverview\nWe are preparing a decision on which candidate distribution centers to activate and how to route product to customers so that all demand is fulfilled at the lowest total delivered cost. The decision balances two primary cost elements: the fixed expense of opening facilities and the variable cost of transportation driven by distance and volume. The analysis uses the facility and customer locations provided, each facility\u2019s available capacity, each customer\u2019s volume requirements, and a uniform per\u2011unit, per\u2011kilometer transport rate.\n\nBusiness Requirements\n- Service coverage: Every customer\u2019s demand must be fully satisfied.\n- Facility activation: Shipments may only depart from facilities that are opened, and opening any facility incurs its associated fixed cost.\n- Capacity discipline: Outbound shipments assigned to any facility must not exceed that facility\u2019s available capacity.\n- Transportation economics: Shipping costs scale with the distance traveled and the quantity shipped, using a consistent per\u2011unit, per\u2011kilometer rate.\n\nCompany Policies (mandatory)\n- Throughput threshold for activation: Any facility that is opened must handle at least 19 units of total outbound shipments across its assigned customers to justify operating overhead.\n- Dependency between specific sites: The location labeled F3 depends operationally on the regional hub labeled F0. If F3 is activated, F0 must also be activated.\n- Oversight limit on network size: To stay within management bandwidth, the company will operate no more than 2 distribution centers at any given time.\n\nDecision Goal\nSelect the set of distribution centers to activate (subject to the oversight limit and the F3\u2013F0 dependency), and assign customer volumes to the opened sites so that:\n- All customer demand is met without breaching any facility\u2019s capacity,\n- Every opened facility handles at least the minimum throughput noted above,\n- Total cost\u2014comprising facility opening costs and transportation costs based on distance and volume\u2014is minimized.\n\nApproach and Deliverables\n- We will evaluate feasible facility combinations that observe the two\u2011site operating limit and the F3\u2013F0 linkage, then allocate shipments from the opened facilities to customers in a way that fully meets demand and respects capacity and minimum\u2011throughput policies.\n- The recommended plan will specify which facilities to open, the customer coverage and shipment volumes from each opened site, and the resulting total cost broken down into fixed and transportation components.\n- We will also highlight the trade\u2011offs that drive the recommendation\u2014for example, when a higher\u2011fixed\u2011cost site could still be preferred due to lower aggregate transport costs\u2014and explain any cases where the minimum\u2011throughput requirement influences site selection.\n\nAnnex: Data Inputs\n- Candidate facility coordinates: {FACILITY_COORDINATES}\n- Customer coordinates: {CUSTOMER_COORDINATES}\n- Facility capacities (units): {FACILITY_CAPACITIES}\n- Customer demands (units): {CUSTOMER_DEMANDS}\n- Facility opening fixed costs: {FIXED_COSTS}\n- Transport rate (per kilometer per unit): {TRANSPORT_RATE}"
